{"page_id": "olmo_long_tiny_text-11_pg146_pg1-p1", "markdown": "# PES\n\nPERSPECTIVE. A reflecting-glass.\n\nPERSPICIL.\n\nAn optic-glass.\n\nIt occurs in\n\nAlbumazar, 1634, sig. B. iv.\n\nPERSTAND.\n\nTo understand. Peele.\n\nPERSUADE.\n\nPersuasion.\n\nPERSUADERS. Spurs.\n\nAlso, pistols.\n\nPERSWAY. To mitigate. Ben Jonson, iv. 428.\n\nPERT.\n\nBeautifully delicate.\n\nIt is the trans-\n\nlation of subtilis in Gesta Rom. p. 142.\n\nFor hete her clothes down sche dede\n\nAlmest to her gerdyl stede, Than lay sche uncovert;\n\nSche was as whyt as lylye yn May, Or snow that sneweth yn wynterys day,\n\nHe seygh never non so pert.\n\nIllustrations of Fairy Mythology, p. 11.\n\nPERTE. (1) To part.\n\nStill in use.\n\nThen Thomas a sory man was he, The terys ran out of his een gray;\n\nLufly lady, get tell thou me\n\nIf we shalle perte for ever and ay.\n\nMS. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f.125.\n\n(2) Of good appearance.\n\nTher was no man in the kynges lande\n\nMore perte then was he.\n\nPERTELICHE.\n\nMS. Cantab. Ff. il. 38, f. 244.\n\nOpenly. (4.-N.)\n\nThan syr Priamous the prynce in presens of lordes Presez to his penowne, and pertly it hentes.\n\nPERTELOTE.\n\nMorte Arthure, MS. Lincoln, f. 84.\n\nThe name of a hen.\n\nPERTENERE. A partner.\n\nGod graunt us mekenesse in angurs here, And grace to lede owre lyfe here soo, That may aftur be pertenere Of hevene, whan we hens schall goo.\n\nMS. Cantab. FE. il. 38, f. 14.\n\nPERTRYCHE. A partridge.\n\nRyght as the pertryche is constreyned undir the claues and nayles of the hauke, is as halfe deed for drede.\n\nCaxton's Divers Pruytful Ghostly Maters.\n\nPERTURBE.\n\nTo trouble.\n\nPaisgrave.\n\nPERTY.\n\nPart. Lydgate.\n\nGod that sittis in Trinité, Gyffe thaym grace wel to the, That lystyns me a whyle;\n\nAlle that lovys of melody,\n\nOff hevon blisse God graunte tham perty,\n\nTheyrr soules shelde fro peryle.\n\nM.S. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f. 47.\n\nPERUR. A kind of cup.\n\nPERUSE.\n\nTo examine, or survey.\n\nMonsleur Soublez having perused the fleet, returned to the king, and told him there was nothing ready; and that the mariners and souldiers would not yeeld to goe the voyage till they were paid thelr\n\nMS. Harl. 383.\n\nPERVEY.\n\nTo provide.\n\nPERVINKE.\n\nThe herb periwinkle. (4.-S.)\n\nPERYE. A pear-tree. (4.-N.)\n\naut sor nur lorae sene aurse not aone, That sate benethe and pleyed hym merye,\n\nBefore the towre undur a perye.\n\nMS. Cantab. Ff. li. 38, f. 141.\n\nPERYSSE.\n\nPears.\n\n(4٠-N.)\n\nThen was the tre ful of ripe perysse, And began down to falle.\n\nMS. Cantab. Ff. V. 48, f.114.\n\nPESAND. A gorget of mail or plate attached\n\n618\n\nPET\n\nto the helmet.\n\n\" A pesane and a paunsone,\"\n\nMS. Morte Arthure, f. 89.\n\nPESATE.\n\nIs when a managed horse rises handsomely before and upon his haunches, and at the same time bends his fore-legs up to his body.\n\nPESE. (1) Peace.\n\nPerceval 980, 981.\n\n(2) To sooth; to appease.\n\nTylle y be sewre of youre hartys ese, Nothing but hit may my grevys pese.\n\nPESEN.\n\nPeas.\n\nMS. Cantab. Ff. i. 6, f. 132.\n\nThis is the common early form\n\nof the word, and occurs in Chaucer, Legende of Good Women, 648.\n\nHolloway gives the\n\nfollowing couplet, as seen lately on a board in a pea-field in Berkshire-\n\nShut the gate after you, I'll tell you the reason, Because the pigs shouldn't get into the peason.\n\nBen Jonson has made the same words rhyme in his 133d epigram.\n\nAs for his sallets, better never was Then acute sorrell, and sweet three-leav'd grasse And for a sawce he seldome is at charges, For every crab-tree doth afford him vergis;\n\nHis banket sometimes is greene beanes and peason, Nuts, peares, plumbes, apples, as they are in season.\n\nPESIBLE.\n\nTaylor's Workes, 1630, 1.97.\n\nPeaceable.\n\n（4.-X）\n\nPESIBLETE.\n\nA calm.\n\n（4.-x）\n\nPESK.\n\nA peach.\n\nNominale MS.\n\nPESON.\n\nAn instrument in the form of a staff, with balls or crockets, used for weighing before scales were employed.\n\nPESS.\n\nA hassock.\n\nSuffolk.\n\nPESSCOD-SCALDING.\n\nA kind of merry-\n\nmaking in summer evenings; the treat, green field peas boiled in the shells.\n\nPESSIPE.\n\nYorksh.\n\nPESTERED.\n\nA kind of cup Peele, i. 235.\n\nCrowded.\n\nPESTERMENT.\n\nEmbarrassment.\n\nNorth.\n\nPESTLE. (1) A leg of an animal, generally of a A pestle of pork is still in common use.\n\nP'Pestels of venison Wrer's Antiq, Culin.\n\np. 98. \" Pestell of flesshe, jambon,\" Palsgrave.\n\nA pestle-pie is a large standing pie which contains a whole gammon, and sometimes a couple of fowls and a neat's tongue, a favorite dish at country fairs, and at Christmas feasts.\n\n(2) A constable's staff.\n\nPESTLE-HEAD.\n\nA blockhead.\n\nPETE. Pity. See Cov. Myst.\n\nLong lay the kyng, there away wolde not hee;\n\nDayly he propherid batayle: the enmys durst not fyghte\n\nLacke of logynge and vitayle it was grett petć, Causid the gentill prynce to remeve, siche was Goddes\n\nmyste I\n\nLowe, how the good Lorde his owne gentill knyzte, Because he shulde remembir hym in wele and in woo, Thus in every thyng, Lorde, thy wille be doo!\n\nMS. Bibl. Rey. 17 D. xv.\n\nPETEOSE.\n\nMerciful; compassionate.\n\nMany men spekes of lamentacioun, Off moders and of thelr gret desolatioun,\n\nWhich that thay did indure\n\nWhen that thelr childer dy and passe, But of his peteose tender moder, alasre!\n\nI am verray sure,\n\nThe wo and payn passis alle othere.\n\nMS. Bodl, e Mus. 1t.", "width": 987, "height": 1612, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "PES", "bbox": {"x": 255.1428569861905, "y": 67.16666658830549, "width": 53.71428571428572, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSPECTIVE. A reflecting-glass.", "bbox": {"x": 67.1428569585792, "y": 110.82499998904892, "width": 339.0714285714286, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSPICIL.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285695401786, "y": 130.97499996851568, "width": 120.85714285714285, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "An optic-glass.", "bbox": {"x": 211.4999996871753, "y": 130.97499994657204, "width": 151.07142857142856, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It occurs in", "bbox": {"x": 372.6428569851732, "y": 130.97499996946976, "width": 124.2142857142857, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Albumazar, 1634, sig. B. iv.", "bbox": {"x": 87.28571411306125, "y": 154.48333331894054, "width": 255.1428571428571, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSTAND.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285696018909, "y": 174.633333303701, "width": 124.21428571428574, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To understand. Peele.", "bbox": {"x": 208.1428572372768, "y": 174.63333328085932, "width": 204.7857142857143, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSUADE.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285696018909, "y": 194.7833333037009, "width": 130.92857142857142, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Persuasion.", "bbox": {"x": 211.24326095013848, "y": 193.3089234466152, "width": 107.94204739161898, "height": 23.09881931145999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSUADERS. Spurs.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285693227275, "y": 218.29166664834852, "width": 231.64285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Also, pistols.", "bbox": {"x": 312.21428555660174, "y": 218.29166663613628, "width": 117.50000000000001, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERSWAY. To mitigate. Ben Jonson, iv. 428.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285697633221, "y": 238.441666657338, "width": 426.3571428571429, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERT.", "bbox": {"x": 66.74328210643553, "y": 257.9944643177909, "width": 68.26857907431466, "height": 22.834092291196033}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Beautifully delicate.", "bbox": {"x": 151.07142745238096, "y": 258.59166627486104, "width": 188, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It is the trans-", "bbox": {"x": 355.85714268519166, "y": 261.94999997952226, "width": 141.00000000000006, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "lation of subtilis in Gesta Rom. p. 142.", "bbox": {"x": 83.92857125748628, "y": 282.09999999031254, "width": 362.5714285714285, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "For hete her clothes down sche dede", "bbox": {"x": 124.21428561755448, "y": 305.6083333162571, "width": 288.7142857142857, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Almest to her gerdyl stede, Than lay sche uncovert;", "bbox": {"x": 127.57142839757651, "y": 325.7583333171, "width": 218.21428571428575, "height": 36.94166666666671}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Sche was as whyt as lylye yn May, Or snow that sneweth yn wynterys day,", "bbox": {"x": 127.36615010967685, "y": 364.4768980477996, "width": 306.0536370958601, "height": 38.68007151285819}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "He seygh never non so pert.", "bbox": {"x": 140.99999983214286, "y": 402.9999999842578, "width": 221.5714285714286, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Illustrations of Fairy Mythology, p. 11.", "bbox": {"x": 198.07142840559382, "y": 419.7916666545281, "width": 302.1428571428571, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTE. (1) To part.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285689322348, "y": 443.2999999698611, "width": 194.71428571428572, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Still in use.", "bbox": {"x": 258.49999972723214, "y": 443.29999993703126, "width": 127.5714285714286, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Then Thomas a sory man was he, The terys ran out of his een gray;", "bbox": {"x": 124.21428552724485, "y": 466.8083333135586, "width": 298.7857142857143, "height": 36.941666666666535}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Lufly lady, get tell thou me", "bbox": {"x": 124.21428549161801, "y": 503.74999998286563, "width": 224.92857142857142, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "If we shalle perte for ever and ay.", "bbox": {"x": 143.97990656510544, "y": 518.7248149628571, "width": 265.9338051932198, "height": 28.82047608693443}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f.125.", "bbox": {"x": 268.5714285612554, "y": 540.6916666361363, "width": 228.28571428571428, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(2) Of good appearance.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285611173469, "y": 560.84166649875, "width": 218.2142857142857, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Ther was no man in the kynges lande", "bbox": {"x": 124.21428554835794, "y": 584.3499999903497, "width": 295.42857142857144, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "More perte then was he.", "bbox": {"x": 124.21428549047617, "y": 601.1416663308333, "width": 188.00000000000003, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTELICHE.", "bbox": {"x": 67.1428569670068, "y": 641.4416666426786, "width": 147.71428571428572, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. il. 38, f. 244.", "bbox": {"x": 265.2142855464285, "y": 621.2916666516294, "width": 231.64285714285714, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Openly. (4.-N.)", "bbox": {"x": 221.57142841086954, "y": 641.4416666447644, "width": 167.8571428571429, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Than syr Priamous the prynce in presens of lordes Presez to his penowne, and pertly it hentes.", "bbox": {"x": 87.28571410654098, "y": 661.5916666567375, "width": 402.8571428571429, "height": 40.299999999999855}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTELOTE.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285687008929, "y": 718.6833332913542, "width": 137.64285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Morte Arthure, MS. Lincoln, f. 84.", "bbox": {"x": 224.92857472976183, "y": 698.5333329975, "width": 271.9285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The name of a hen.", "bbox": {"x": 214.8571426625812, "y": 718.6833333104356, "width": 184.64285714285717, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTENERE. A partner.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285689600842, "y": 742.1916666469119, "width": 251.78571428571428, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "God graunt us mekenesse in angurs here, And grace to lede owre lyfe here soo, That may aftur be pertenere Of hevene, whan we hens schall goo.", "bbox": {"x": 107.42857167710032, "y": 762.3416666166612, "width": 325.64285714285717, "height": 80.60000000000007}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. FE. il. 38, f. 14.", "bbox": {"x": 288.7142855491803, "y": 839.5833333195696, "width": 208.1428571428571, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTRYCHE. A partridge.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285695634925, "y": 863.0916666503414, "width": 268.57142857142856, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Ryght as the pertryche is constreyned undir the claues and nayles of the hauke, is as halfe deed for drede.", "bbox": {"x": 90.39228744138344, "y": 884.027004705846, "width": 406.806624003819, "height": 59.89725871880855}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Caxton's Divers Pruytful Ghostly Maters.", "bbox": {"x": 187.8209853059125, "y": 922.7817731690674, "width": 309.2044290815081, "height": 24.22226293087002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTURBE.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285696512606, "y": 947.0499999703676, "width": 127.57142857142857, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To trouble.", "bbox": {"x": 204.65260990541827, "y": 946.2898866174378, "width": 111.05192266191757, "height": 21.670225884516988}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Paisgrave.", "bbox": {"x": 322.2312351069009, "y": 946.7982992850826, "width": 107.53752899169919, "height": 24.01173455317807}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERTY.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285696737014, "y": 970.5583332951705, "width": 83.92857142857143, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Part. Lydgate.", "bbox": {"x": 161.1428569661654, "y": 970.55833330682, "width": 147.71428571428575, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "God that sittis in Trinité, Gyffe thaym grace wel to the, That lystyns me a whyle;", "bbox": {"x": 127.57142839085496, "y": 990.7083333182516, "width": 238.35714285714283, "height": 57.09166666666664}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Alle that lovys of melody,", "bbox": {"x": 127.12059119045733, "y": 1041.541796691544, "width": 209.3537998199463, "height": 30.101998146374974}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Off hevon blisse God graunte tham perty,", "bbox": {"x": 127.39983076349978, "y": 1063.3874116428628, "width": 316.0078479221889, "height": 25.358315801620375}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Theyrr soules shelde fro peryle.", "bbox": {"x": 147.7142855441292, "y": 1088.0999999861988, "width": 248.4285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "M.S. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f. 47.", "bbox": {"x": 278.6428569749999, "y": 1104.8916666506746, "width": 218.21428571428575, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERUR. A kind of cup.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999979617347, "y": 1125.041666645677, "width": 228.28571428571428, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERUSE.", "bbox": {"x": 70.35526522321459, "y": 1144.598430956423, "width": 94.28947135380336, "height": 24.694803992907147}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To examine, or survey.", "bbox": {"x": 177.6278497293415, "y": 1144.892981050774, "width": 212.15817642211917, "height": 24.286629523833724}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Monsleur Soublez having perused the fleet, returned to the king, and told him there was nothing ready; and that the mariners and souldiers would not yeeld to goe the voyage till they were paid thelr", "bbox": {"x": 89.77269270416959, "y": 1167.6929154849986, "width": 410.9750832148961, "height": 86.20224841435757}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Harl. 383.", "bbox": {"x": 382.71428552244896, "y": 1245.9416666306845, "width": 114.14285714285711, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERVEY.", "bbox": {"x": 70.24178924262065, "y": 1268.2884218653803, "width": 101.23070716857912, "height": 25.831489408016132}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To provide.", "bbox": {"x": 177.80511034240706, "y": 1268.8718239829275, "width": 107.67549324035643, "height": 24.664686073859592}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERVINKE.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999982720587, "y": 1292.958333303701, "width": 124.21428571428571, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The herb periwinkle. (4.-S.)", "bbox": {"x": 208.14285703577588, "y": 1289.599999979734, "width": 271.9285714285714, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERYE. A pear-tree. (4.-N.)", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999983214283, "y": 1313.1083333211948, "width": 285.35714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "aut sor nur lorae sene aurse not aone, That sate benethe and pleyed hym merye,", "bbox": {"x": 107.42857129487666, "y": 1339.9749999897435, "width": 335.71428571428567, "height": 33.583333333333215}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Before the towre undur a perye.", "bbox": {"x": 107.42857118830534, "y": 1373.5583333168709, "width": 251.78571428571425, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. li. 38, f. 141.", "bbox": {"x": 271.92857138660713, "y": 1390.3499999720138, "width": 224.92857142857147, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PERYSSE.", "bbox": {"x": 70.38632307359977, "y": 1409.915079793397, "width": 100.94163921901158, "height": 21.319840347766768}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Pears.", "bbox": {"x": 177.90201663846548, "y": 1410.406630597423, "width": 70.55310848781043, "height": 20.336738304297143}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(4٠-N.)", "bbox": {"x": 261.8571430669643, "y": 1410.499999706146, "width": 77.2142857142857, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Then was the tre ful of ripe perysse, And began down to falle.", "bbox": {"x": 126.92434179300359, "y": 1430.1521969354428, "width": 286.47671127319336, "height": 42.70361891984947}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. V. 48, f.114.", "bbox": {"x": 271.92857126071425, "y": 1470.9499999870834, "width": 224.9285714285715, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESAND. A gorget of mail or plate attached", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999983214286, "y": 1491.0999999907447, "width": 426.3571428571429, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "618", "bbox": {"x": 483.4285712467262, "y": 67.16666658270827, "width": 43.64285714285714, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PET", "bbox": {"x": 701.6428573442857, "y": 63.8083330646666, "width": 53.714285714285666, "height": 26.86666666666675}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "to the helmet.", "bbox": {"x": 533.7857139947617, "y": 107.46666659949997, "width": 134.28571428571433, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "\" A pesane and a paunsone,\"", "bbox": {"x": 664.714285552803, "y": 107.46666665391356, "width": 275.2857142857144, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Morte Arthure, f. 89.", "bbox": {"x": 533.7857141153887, "y": 130.97499998765326, "width": 231.64285714285708, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESATE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571411140103, "y": 151.12499996125004, "width": 90.64285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Is when a managed horse rises handsomely before and upon his haunches, and at the same time bends his fore-legs up to his body.", "bbox": {"x": 530.4285712534792, "y": 151.12499989454616, "width": 412.92857142857144, "height": 63.808333333333465}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESE. (1) Peace.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857140568182, "y": 214.93333330280296, "width": 157.78571428571436, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Perceval 980, 981.", "bbox": {"x": 681.4999997952962, "y": 214.9333333046646, "width": 174.57142857142856, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(2) To sooth; to appease.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428562906593, "y": 235.08333324291664, "width": 228.28571428571422, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Tylle y be sewre of youre hartys ese, Nothing but hit may my grevys pese.", "bbox": {"x": 587.4999997708617, "y": 258.59166665221227, "width": 295.42857142857144, "height": 40.30000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESEN.", "bbox": {"x": 510.216456646823, "y": 315.4143978443447, "width": 77.35280064174098, "height": 20.687870883941578}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Peas.", "bbox": {"x": 597.5714280678571, "y": 315.6833330814583, "width": 60.42857142857139, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. i. 6, f. 132.", "bbox": {"x": 725.1428655603846, "y": 295.5333329975, "width": 214.85713005065912, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "This is the common early form", "bbox": {"x": 661.3571423097826, "y": 315.6833332895291, "width": 278.6428571428571, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "of the word, and occurs in Chaucer, Legende of Good Women, 648.", "bbox": {"x": 530.2038602810511, "y": 335.6290257769226, "width": 413.2776121412005, "height": 45.643696308135986}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Holloway gives the", "bbox": {"x": 758.2718346009298, "y": 358.0851753110139, "width": 185.42082541329523, "height": 26.94218445618957}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "following couplet, as seen lately on a board in a pea-field in Berkshire-", "bbox": {"x": 533.3544683835931, "y": 377.45220285707285, "width": 406.9385692051479, "height": 46.29758703708649}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Shut the gate after you, I'll tell you the reason, Because the pigs shouldn't get into the peason.", "bbox": {"x": 530.4285712187499, "y": 423.1499999888001, "width": 386.07142857142856, "height": 40.299999999999855}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Ben Jonson has made the same words rhyme in his 133d epigram.", "bbox": {"x": 529.8585292070752, "y": 457.00049244813005, "width": 413.86562183925076, "height": 56.13387280305222}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "As for his sallets, better never was Then acute sorrell, and sweet three-leav'd grasse And for a sawce he seldome is at charges, For every crab-tree doth afford him vergis;", "bbox": {"x": 529.6442731414714, "y": 506.06219907440106, "width": 393.9334313528878, "height": 82.14488790829975}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "His banket sometimes is greene beanes and peason, Nuts, peares, plumbes, apples, as they are in season.", "bbox": {"x": 529.9196478292026, "y": 581.0510912458795, "width": 403.7230276380266, "height": 47.196547869841126}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESIBLE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571409920636, "y": 641.4416666293519, "width": 107.42857142857133, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Taylor's Workes, 1630, 1.97.", "bbox": {"x": 725.1428567064286, "y": 621.2916666263668, "width": 218.21428571428575, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Peaceable.", "bbox": {"x": 624.428573119478, "y": 641.4416663308333, "width": 104.07142216818676, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "（4.-X）", "bbox": {"x": 728.5000005035715, "y": 641.4416662748612, "width": 83.92857142857142, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESIBLETE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2615291170411, "y": 661.4596233883682, "width": 127.61979866027832, "height": 23.772419802347724}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A calm.", "bbox": {"x": 651.2857140619049, "y": 664.9499999440279, "width": 80.57142857142856, "height": 16.79166666666643}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "（4.-x）", "bbox": {"x": 744.8112335583788, "y": 661.5916665040806, "width": 71.40977260044636, "height": 22.3338746110598}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESK.", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571411785725, "y": 685.0999999407354, "width": 63.78571428571425, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A peach.", "bbox": {"x": 580.5374288616988, "y": 686.048382421712, "width": 94.41394397190646, "height": 23.09956635435421}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Nominale MS.", "bbox": {"x": 688.2142855464286, "y": 685.0999999727704, "width": 130.92857142857147, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESON.", "bbox": {"x": 510.23996614838006, "y": 705.0731165254891, "width": 77.30578163691928, "height": 20.503766846656763}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "An instrument in the form of a staff, with balls or crockets, used for weighing before scales were employed.", "bbox": {"x": 530.3452324444107, "y": 707.1560091165328, "width": 409.9305864061629, "height": 66.71366241772972}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESS.", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571411785714, "y": 772.4166666141926, "width": 60.42857142857139, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A hassock.", "bbox": {"x": 587.4999998256868, "y": 772.4166666279167, "width": 104.07142857142847, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Suffolk.", "bbox": {"x": 708.3571426981202, "y": 772.4166666136404, "width": 67.14285714285722, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESSCOD-SCALDING.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857175309523, "y": 789.2083329415276, "width": 228.2857142857143, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A kind of merry-", "bbox": {"x": 755.0775020002574, "y": 790.3316613094282, "width": 188.66414424351285, "height": 26.30136097272229}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "making in summer evenings; the treat, green field peas boiled in the shells.", "bbox": {"x": 533.7857140507142, "y": 816.074999985753, "width": 409.5714285714286, "height": 40.30000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESSIPE.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569968944, "y": 856.3749999561954, "width": 94, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Yorksh.", "bbox": {"x": 819.1428563035715, "y": 836.224999748125, "width": 73.85714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESTERED.", "bbox": {"x": 510.285714117857, "y": 879.883333303701, "width": 120.85714285714288, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A kind of cup Peele, i. 235.", "bbox": {"x": 618.587146484829, "y": 844.2850007760053, "width": 260.3799918038504, "height": 72.6743312835694}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Crowded.", "bbox": {"x": 651.285714103869, "y": 879.8833332913541, "width": 87.28571428571428, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESTERMENT.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857141100498, "y": 900.0333333059981, "width": 157.78571428571425, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Embarrassment.", "bbox": {"x": 674.7857120476191, "y": 900.0333329975002, "width": 154.4285714285715, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "North.", "bbox": {"x": 842.642856965126, "y": 903.3916666172796, "width": 67.14285714285711, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESTLE. (1) A leg of an animal, generally of a A pestle of pork is still in common use.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857140464697, "y": 923.5416666546109, "width": 429.71428571428567, "height": 40.30000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "P'Pestels of venison Wrer's Antiq, Culin.", "bbox": {"x": 530.4285692277779, "y": 947.0499997761111, "width": 409.5714285714286, "height": 40.30000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "p. 98. \" Pestell of flesshe, jambon,\" Palsgrave.", "bbox": {"x": 533.7857141006409, "y": 987.3499999849304, "width": 402.8571428571429, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A pestle-pie is a large standing pie which contains a whole gammon, and sometimes a couple of fowls and a neat's tongue, a favorite dish at country fairs, and at Christmas feasts.", "bbox": {"x": 530.2331399626579, "y": 1010.8131818042414, "width": 413.2887537819999, "height": 87.53232425848648}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(2) A constable's staff.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569750001, "y": 1094.8166666495904, "width": 204.7857142857143, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PESTLE-HEAD.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857117119049, "y": 1114.9666663308335, "width": 161.1428571428571, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A blockhead.", "bbox": {"x": 684.8571426988775, "y": 1118.3249999712143, "width": 124.21428571428574, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PETE. Pity. See Cov. Myst.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857140914796, "y": 1138.4749999856072, "width": 278.6428571428571, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Long lay the kyng, there away wolde not hee;", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857139157433, "y": 1161.983333312772, "width": 369.2857142857144, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Dayly he propherid batayle: the enmys durst not fyghte", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569667447, "y": 1182.133333325075, "width": 429.71428571428567, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Lacke of logynge and vitayle it was grett petć, Causid the gentill prynce to remeve, siche was Goddes", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571411094566, "y": 1202.2833333233336, "width": 429.7142857142858, "height": 36.941666666666535}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "myste I", "bbox": {"x": 546.3230105059664, "y": 1238.3334071135835, "width": 65.90991933005192, "height": 23.70151077906299}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Lowe, how the good Lorde his owne gentill knyzte, Because he shulde remembir hym in wele and in woo, Thus in every thyng, Lorde, thy wille be doo!", "bbox": {"x": 510.0825415305284, "y": 1258.100035643761, "width": 423.41797801426475, "height": 59.66235896746315}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Bibl. Rey. 17 D. xv.", "bbox": {"x": 741.9285712205746, "y": 1316.4666666447645, "width": 198.07142857142867, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PETEOSE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.285714110863, "y": 1333.2583332843578, "width": 117.50000000000001, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Merciful; compassionate.", "bbox": {"x": 624.4285712171959, "y": 1336.6166666448996, "width": 234.99999999999994, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Many men spekes of lamentacioun, Off moders and of thelr gret desolatioun,", "bbox": {"x": 567.1304115576744, "y": 1355.1271234609876, "width": 316.1597584315709, "height": 42.05879999796551}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Which that thay did indure", "bbox": {"x": 604.285714059472, "y": 1393.708333311431, "width": 221.5714285714286, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "When that thelr childer dy and passe, But of his peteose tender moder, alasre!", "bbox": {"x": 567.0963610496482, "y": 1412.1231150380122, "width": 316.09558514186307, "height": 44.870672655105736}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "I am verray sure,", "bbox": {"x": 603.905603654495, "y": 1451.496628172207, "width": 141.92850848606665, "height": 23.107772616545336}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The wo and payn passis alle othere.", "bbox": {"x": 570.7142855260134, "y": 1470.9499999863851, "width": 278.6428571428571, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Bodl, e Mus. 1t.", "bbox": {"x": 772.1428569677018, "y": 1491.0999999780977, "width": 173.73214285714292, "height": 20.149999999999928}}], "ms": 434.293917}